  <name>DriveDeck for OneDrive</name>
  <summary>The easiest, most complete way to use OneDrive</summary>
  <replaces>
    <id>io.github.sweatshopking.LinuxOnedriveGui</id>
  </replaces>
  <description>
    <p>
      The easiest, most complete way to use OneDrive on Linux: a friendly front end for the
      OneDrive Client for Linux, which it installs for you if it's missing. Sign in with your Microsoft account, pick which folders to keep on your computer, and
      keep them in sync in the background.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Personal, work or school OneDrive accounts and SharePoint libraries</li>
      <li>Tray icon with live status, recent files, pause and "sync now"</li>
      <li>Choose folders, set sync schedules and speed limits</li>
      <li>Preview of every full resync before anything changes</li>
      <li>Copy sharing links from the file manager</li>
    </ul>
    <p>DriveDeck used to be called "A GUI that works with OneDrive on Linux".</p>
    <p>Not made by or affiliated with Microsoft. OneDrive is a trademark of Microsoft.</p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">drivedeck.desktop</launchable>
